package lattice:plugin-host@0.1.0;

/// OA.14d fixture world — **org's exact shape**, reduced to the two seams that
/// make the bug possible: a component that DECLARES an option (`config`) and
/// then READS it from a load-time export (`theme`).
///
/// That combination is what `pre-plugin-loaded` exists for. `plugin-loaded`
/// fires after both have run, so a handler using it sets a value nothing will
/// consult again until a restart — which is precisely how org's
/// `todo-keyword-styles` came to have no effect. A fixture with only one of the
/// two seams cannot show the difference between a load that waited for the
/// handler and one that did not.
///
/// The element it registers is NAMED AFTER the option's value, so the theme
/// registry records what the guest actually saw at load. An assertion on a
/// registered name is not defeatable by ordering luck the way "the option now
/// holds the right value" would be — that would still pass if the set landed a
/// microsecond after the read.
world preload-fixture {
    import config;
    import theme;

    export register-options: func();
    export register-theme-elements: func();
}
